What I would prioritize next

Since you're building this for your portfolio, I'd focus on:

Split Dashboard.jsx into smaller components if it's getting large.
Create reusable components for forms, tables, and modals.
Add utils for formatting currency, dates, and validation.
Replace the default Vite favicon with a custom finance-themed icon (wallet, chart, or coin).
Introduce a shared styles folder or a design system so your UI has a consistent look across all pages.

These changes will improve both the maintainability of your code and the overall polish of the project.



































This is actually where many beginner React projects differ from professional ones. A good React project has small, reusable components, not one giant Dashboard.jsx.

